  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#4879\", \"PowerToys#5001\", \"PowerToys#34383\"], \"answer\": \"Someone has already asked for this. A hotkey to toggle Keyboard Manager on and off is tracked in PowerToys#4879. Later requests, such as #34383, were closed as duplicates of it. The archive doesn't say the feature has been built, so there's no built-in shortcut yet. Two workarounds are described in #4879. (1) Use a small PowerShell script that stops the PowerToys.KeyboardManagerEngine process if it's running, or starts it if it isn't. Bind the script to a hotkey with a desktop shortcut's 'Shortcut key' setting, or with AutoHotkey. The PowerToys settings page may not show the right on/off state while you do this. (2) Suggested in the ticket as an idea: toggle it from the PowerToys Run PowerToys plugin. The archive doesn't say whether that exists. You can add your scenario to #4879.\"}",
